# Liquid Storage Manager

Before writing code, read and follow [AGENT.md](AGENT.md), [docs/SRS.md](docs/SRS.md), and [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md). Those three files are the coding, scaling, and structure contract. This file repeats them so either entrypoint stays aligned. If a change moves a boundary, update the docs in the same change. Do not leave the implementation smarter than the docs, or the docs ahead of the code.

If this file and those docs ever disagree, follow the docs and update this file.

## Forbidden drift

- Sending the full recursive tree to the webview
- Rendering more than `GRAPH_CHILD_CAP` (60) child spheres
- Calling `@tauri-apps/api` or `tauri-remote-ui` outside `src/services/tauriBridge.ts`
- `.unwrap()` / `.expect()` in commands or services (`Builder::run` in `lib.rs` is the one allowed startup `.expect()`)
- `setState` inside `useFrame`
- `std::fs::remove_file` / `remove_dir_all` outside `permanent_delete`
- A second cache that mixes filtered search results, insight pages, reclaim rows, duplicate groups, or growth deltas into the tree pages
- Reclaim or duplicate review calling `permanent_delete`
- Duplicate results that include a never-delete prefix, including Windows caches
- Treating the growth snapshot as a second tree or sending it wholesale to the webview
- Raising `GRAPH_CHILD_CAP` for the area map

## Architecture

- `src-tauri/src/commands/` contains only thin Tauri command wrappers. Scanning, size aggregation, and OS operations belong in `src-tauri/src/services/`.
- `src/components/explorer/` is 2D UI only. `src/components/visualizer/` is 3D only.
- Frontend components never call `@tauri-apps/api` or `tauri-remote-ui`. IPC goes through `src/services/tauriBridge.ts`. `invoke` and `listen` come from `tauri-remote-ui`. `Channel` stays on `@tauri-apps/api`.
- Zustand (`src/store/useFileStore.ts`) is the only shared frontend state.
- Rust `ScanIndex` owns the full tree. JavaScript holds the open branch, one folder page, and the current graph view.
- Do not return the recursive tree. Progress every 100ms carries the root plus at most 200 direct children. `get_children` pages (default 400, clamp 1000). `get_graph_view` returns the focus, at most 60 children, and one aggregate.
- Normalize Windows paths in `services/paths.rs` before storing or sending them. One function. No ad-hoc slash logic.
- An elevated NTFS drive root is read with `MftScan`. Every other scan uses `FindFirstFileExW` with `FIND_FIRST_EX_LARGE_FETCH` and takes size from the find buffer. Do not stat each file again. Scan hidden files. Do not follow symlinks or reparse points. Do not descend `System Volume Information` or `$Recycle.Bin`. Count other access errors and continue. A non-elevated launch with a fixed NTFS drive asks once whether to restart as administrator. A debug restart exits and starts an elevated `tauri dev`. A release build exits and leaves one elevated process. Normal and elevated runs use separate WebView2 data directories.
- Heavy work uses `tauri::async_runtime::spawn_blocking`. Stream `ScanProgress` on `tauri::ipc::Channel` in the webview, and emit `scan-progress` with `EmitterExt` for the browser socket. The browser command returns immediately and the page waits for `done`. The remote-ui server starts only in debug builds. The scanner takes a progress callback so tests do not need a Tauri runtime.
- Cancel with `Arc<AtomicBool>` (relaxed). A generation counter stops an older scan from overwriting a newer index. On cancel, keep the partial index and return `Ok` with `cancelled: true`.
- `trash_path` uses the `trash` crate. Never delete a drive root (`C:\`). Reclaim and duplicate review never call `permanent_delete`. Duplicate results never include never-delete prefixes, and they have no Windows-cache exception. Insight results never merge into `childPages`. The growth file is not the tree. The area map does not raise `GRAPH_CHILD_CAP`.
- `notify` watches the focused folder non-recursively, or the parent folder when a file is focused, debounces, and emits `fs-stale`. It does not start a scan.
- `AppError` (`thiserror`) serializes as a string. Commands return `Result<T, AppError>`.
- Rust structs use `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]`. TypeScript mirrors live in `src/types/filesystem.ts`. No `any`.
- Keep files under about 250 lines. New constants go in `src-tauri/src/limits.rs` and `src/lib/limits.ts`, then into `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- New IPC is unfinished until the command, the bridge function, and the TypeScript type all exist.
- Stay on the React version already in `package.json`. Virtualize lists. Keep tree pages and the filtered folder list in separate caches. Focus pages ancestors from the scan root downward.
- In `useFrame`, write refs and uniforms. Read the store with `useFileStore.getState()`. Do not uncapped the 60-sphere graph. No bloom pass unless `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` records a measured FPS note. `OrganicGraph2D` calls `finishDrain` once when a drain ends.
